  "status": "proposed",
  "why": "The seed holds as given: the crane is turn 2's second way with its price attached, and a dig whose find is already photographed and cracked is the agent's dig from that minute on. The seed's ending world holds: the foreman stays for his nephew's sake, the student goes with the find.",
  "through_line": {
    "title": "The Sponsor's Hill",
    "motivation": "The crane has the nephew out in a minute and the agent has his photograph of the cracked lid. You come to want the dig finished at any price, because the find is already half his and the rain is not waiting; by the end you want only to be the one who signed, so that the foreman's men were paid for it.",
    "strategy": "Take the agent's money and his crew, keep the foreman's men on by paying them from it, and get the find to the station before the council can organize.",
    "turning_point": "The agent's pay book. Once the foreman's men are drawing his wages through your hand, every order you give at the trench is his, and you give them anyway.",
    "differs_from": "T1 keeps the find on the hill and pays with the student; this line gives the other answer: the find leaves cracked in the sponsor's crate, the student with it, and the foreman stays only because his nephew is alive and his men were paid, in a dig that stopped being yours at the second crisis."
  },
  "divergence": {
    "diverges_at": "N02",
    "trigger": "you let the agent swing his crane over the trench to get the nephew out",
    "trigger_kind": "act",
    "way": 2,
    "instead_of": "the foreman's men dug the nephew out by hand while you held the lamp",
    "opportunity": null,
    "shift": "The nephew is out alive in a minute, by the agent's machine, and the foreman's men have seen whose hand it was. The crane's foot has cracked the find's lid, the agent has his photograph, and from here the dig runs on his pay book."
  },
  "ending": { "title": "The Cracked Lid", "summary": "The find leaves on the train in the sponsor's crate with its lid cracked, and the student rides with it to put her name on the catalogue. The foreman stays on the hill with his men paid and his nephew alive, and does not come down to the station.",
              "answer": "pole_a", "standing": ["the foreman"], "lost": ["the student"], "changed": "the find is the sponsor's and damaged; the village never saw it" },
  "beats": [
    { "beat": "third_crisis", "turn": 3, "way": 2, "event": null, "adapted": "The agent's hired crew is on the hill by morning and the foreman's men stand back from the trench until you tell them the agent's money is their pay. You let the student certify the find for export, in the arm sling, with the agent's pen; the men go down for the agent's wages, and the foreman watches you give the order and says nothing." },
    { "beat": "climax", "turn": 4, "way": 2, "event": 2, "adapted": "The sponsor's crate is on the platform before the find is clean, and the council is on the road with the foreman's mother at the front. You sign the export form on the crate's lid and the student climbs into the goods van beside it; the foreman has not come down from the hill, and his mother turns back when she sees your name on the form." },
    { "beat": "aftermath", "turn": null, "way": null, "event": null, "adapted": "The train is gone with the find and the student, and the agent's photograph of the cracked lid will be in the sponsor's catalogue before your report. The foreman's men are paid to the day; the village church has an empty table where the council meant to put the find, and nobody on the hill asks when you are leaving." }
