(Three new entries, starting at the beat after the divergence node's;
turns 3 and 4 played once each, by ways T1 did not take, so no node is
retold; event 2 lands here as it did on T1 but goes the other way; the
agent acts in the third crisis with his crew and his pay book; the ending
answers the question with pole_a and names who stands and who is lost,
and the foreman's standing is paid for in the third crisis. Every
required beat is on the path, so skipped_beats is empty.)

USER INPUT FOLLOWS BELOW

- the Kernel
$$KERNEL$$

- the brief (decision, theme, affect, failure)
$$BRIEF_LITE_JSON$$

- the engine: protagonist, pressure, opposition, events (numbered), cast (with voices and breaking points), question and poles, levers, turns (ways numbered), complications
$$PREMISE_JSON$$

- the promises (defaults; the Kernel and the brief beat them)
$$PROMISES$$

- the framework and its beats
$$FRAMEWORK_JSON$$

- the craft spine: want, need, the tension between them (or none). A new line may answer the need differently from the lines before it.
$$CRAFT_JSON$$

- the story so far (one entry per node)
$$STORY_DIGEST_JSON$$

- ways through a turn that no line has taken
$$HOOKS_JSON$$

- THE SEED for this line
$$SEED_JSON$$
